# roadmaps/realtime.md R0 across processes' ends (roadmap l4.md L12, L13;
# os-server.md P12): processes killed and ended, everything made for each
# revoked a capability at a time with a window after each (ROOT_EXIT),
# others made; the kernel still never keeps interrupts off for half a
# tick. Without the windows an end is one stretch over every slot of every
# space, for each capability it deletes. (Before P12: the clock's module,
# killed and started again by the old shell.)
program: shell
define: TEST_STRETCH
install: C /BIN/SLEEP z-sleep.rx
install: C /BIN/KILL z-kill.rx
keys: {wait 50}sleep 30 &\nsleep 30 &\n{wait 20}kill 10 11\n{wait 50}ls /z | cat\n{wait 50}
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
---
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
